{
  "_about": "Design tokens for Ziy \u2014 a privacy-first browser UI built from the measured reference screenshots in replica/screens/. Roles are named for what a colour DOES; replica-brand only changes values. Every text/UI pair is checked with: python3 contrast.py replica/design/tokens.json. Ziy's signature colour is its own (see _accent-note); the original's accent is recorded only as a role and is never reused.",
  "_accent-note": "The original's recorded accent was a cobalt/indigo blue (#434fcf family). It is deliberately NOT reused. Ziy's signature colour is GLOOM TEAL #0b6e6e (light) / #2dd4bf (dark): a deep cyan-teal. Rationale: (1) it reads as 'sealed / quiet / watertight' \u2014 a shield-and-guard identity without borrowing anyone's lion or orange; (2) it sits opposite the warm greys measured from the reference (bg #ffffff, surface #fafafb, border #e4e4e5), so accent-on-neutral contrast survives at AA on every surface we use; (3) teal is unclaimed in this category \u2014 chrome blue, red, orange and violet are all taken by other products; (4) the light value clears 4.5:1 on white/surface AND carries white text at 6.05:1, so one accent value serves both text-on-bg and bg-with-on-accent without a second hue.",
  "_measurement-note": "All neutral values measured from replica/screens/*.png with PIL on 2026-10-14: white #ffffff (page/av), surface #fafafb (settings content pane), #f8f8f9 / #f0f0f0 (sunken chrome and divider fills), #e4e4e5 (1px card border), #c9c9ca and #8b8b8b (input/toggle and mid-grey), text #202124, secondary text #6e6e6e/#5f6368 family, muted-grey #1c1c1d. Chrome layout measured: 64px toolbar band, 240px settings nav, 2px accent focus ring, 10px card radius. NTP widget fills measured from brave.png (search box ~#bdbcc1 hairline, stats card ~#cfcfdb translucent, credit pill ~#c6c9dc) \u2014 these inform the frosted-glass role, not the shipped palette.",
